+<tr><td>Systems</td><td>Plans maintained-record integrations with ERP, PLM, LCA and compliance systems. <!-- CHECK: 05-circularise --></td><td>Provider neutrality may matter: one canonical export and test suite can target several passport hosts.</td></tr>
+</tbody></table></div>
+<p>Neutrality, second-life lineage and managed exceptions are hypotheses, not established moats. Circularise may satisfy all three through its native workflow or services. A customer's ERP team may also generate the payload at source. <!-- CHECK: 05-erp-substitute --> Formal interoperability increases that pressure. The Regulation requires transferable data without vendor lock-in. <!-- CHECK: 05-operator-responsibility --> The registry indexes rather than stores the complete record. <!-- CHECK: 05-registry-live --> Those rules protect exit but commoditise translation.</p>
+<p>Use an incumbent to reach production, while keeping customer-controlled export and a provider-neutral test suite. Kill this offer if two qualified buyers accept Circularise's native workflow, without paid external exception management, after testing their real second-life data. In that case, an entrant would duplicate a product rather than own a neglected operation.</p>
 </section>
 
